{#
  Shared body for the four legal-page routes (/impressum/, /en/imprint/,
  /datenschutz/, /en/privacy/). Phase 3F: STRUCTURE ONLY -- no legal wording
  is written anywhere in this partial or the two data files it reads
  (impressumPage.js / datenschutzPage.js). Deliberately simpler than the
  commercial pages: page-hero, one confirmed-facts block, then a flat list
  of sections -- no cards, no grids, no color blocks. Text-oriented content
  gets a text-oriented layout; this is not a new visual language, it's the
  existing typography/spacing/border tokens used more sparingly.

  Include with `legal` set to either impressumPage[lang] or
  datenschutzPage[lang] before this partial, e.g.:
    {%- set legal = impressumPage[lang] -%}
    {% include "partials/legal-body.njk" %}

  CONFIRMED-FACTS BLOCK: reads company.legalName/legalForm/address/email
  directly through the `required` filter (eleventy.config.js) -- the single
  source those facts already have everywhere else on the site. If one of
  them were ever nulled out again, the build fails loudly instead of
  quietly publishing a blank or a guess. Telephone is never rendered here:
  company.phone is null on purpose and there is no pending line for it,
  because there will never be a value to fill in (Phase 3A business rule).

  SECTION LIST: each `legal.sections[]` entry is {id, heading, body, list,
  configKey?}. `body` is null until real legal text exists -- rendered as
  the real heading plus an honest "not written yet" status note
  (ui.legalPending), never invented prose and never a bracket placeholder
  like "[STEUERNUMMER]". A `configKey` gates the whole section on whether
  that tool is actually configured (site.forms.turnstileSiteKey /
  site.analytics.configured) -- the same "render nothing when unconfigured"
  rule already used by consent-head.njk and the contact form, so this page
  can never claim a tool is active that isn't.

  `body` may be a single string (one <p>), or an array whose entries are
  rendered in order -- a string becomes a <p>, an array becomes a <ul><li>
  bullet list at that exact position (so a section can read: paragraph,
  list, paragraph, in whatever order the real legal text needs). Same
  text-soft/text-base typography throughout -- not a new visual language,
  just the semantically correct elements for genuinely list-shaped content
  (data categories, rights, recipients) interleaved with real prose.
#}
{%- set t = ui[lang] -%}
{%- set heroEyebrow = legal.eyebrow -%}
{%- set heroH1 = legal.h -%}
{% include "partials/page-hero.njk" %}

<section class="row row--no-border">
  <div class="container stack" style="max-width:42em;gap:var(--space-lg)">

    {%- if legal.translationNote %}
    <p class="text-faint" style="font-size:var(--text-sm);font-style:italic">{{ legal.translationNote }}</p>
    {%- endif %}

    <div class="stack" style="gap:12px">
      <h2 style="font-size:var(--text-2xl)">{{ legal.operatorHeading }}</h2>
      <div class="stack" style="gap:2px">
        <span class="eyebrow" style="color:var(--color-text-faint)">{{ t.legalFields.name }}</span>
        <span>{{ company.legalName | required("legalName") }}</span>
      </div>
      <div class="stack" style="gap:2px">
        <span class="eyebrow" style="color:var(--color-text-faint)">{{ t.legalFields.form }}</span>
        <span>{{ company.legalForm | required("legalForm") }}</span>
      </div>
      <div class="stack" style="gap:2px">
        <span class="eyebrow" style="color:var(--color-text-faint)">{{ t.legalFields.address }}</span>
        <span>{{ company.address.street | required("address.street") }}<br>{{ company.address.postalCode | required("address.postalCode") }} {{ company.address.city | required("address.city") }}</span>
      </div>
      <div class="stack" style="gap:2px">
        <span class="eyebrow" style="color:var(--color-text-faint)">{{ t.legalFields.email }}</span>
        <a href="mailto:{{ company.email | required('email') }}">{{ company.email }}</a>
      </div>
    </div>

    {%- for s in legal.sections %}
      {%- if not s.configKey
          or (s.configKey == "turnstile" and site.forms.turnstileSiteKey)
          or (s.configKey == "analytics" and site.analytics.configured) %}
    <div class="stack" style="gap:8px;border-top:1px solid var(--color-border-soft);padding-top:var(--space-lg)">
      <h2 style="font-size:var(--text-xl)">{{ s.heading }}</h2>
      {%- if s.body %}
        {%- for block in ([s.body] if s.body is string else s.body) %}
          {%- if block is string %}
      <p class="text-soft" style="font-size:var(--text-base);line-height:var(--leading-relaxed)">{{ block }}</p>
          {%- else %}
      <ul class="text-soft" style="font-size:var(--text-base);line-height:var(--leading-relaxed);padding-left:1.25em;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:4px">
            {%- for item in block %}
        <li>{{ item }}</li>
            {%- endfor %}
      </ul>
          {%- endif %}
        {%- endfor %}
      {%- else %}
      <p class="text-faint" style="font-size:var(--text-sm);font-style:italic">{{ t.legalPending }}</p>
      {%- endif %}
    </div>
      {%- endif %}
    {%- endfor %}

  </div>
</section>
